LOCUS       order_loc                500 bp    DNA     circular SYN 28-APR-2026
DEFINITION  Synthetic plasmid for the order() guard regression in
            applyComplementOriginWrap. NOT a real construct.
ACCESSION   order_boundary_synth
VERSION     order_boundary_synth
COMMENT     regression fixture for the order() guard. `order(...)` has
            different semantics from `join(...)` — parts are biologically
            ordered but not joined into one contiguous gene. The
            origin-wrap detection must NOT fire for order() even when the
            parts happen to touch the sequence boundaries. Without the
            order() guard, complement(order(1..50,451..500)) would be
            silently rewritten to start>end shape with segments in physical
            order — the wrong representation for an order() location.
FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     CDS             complement(order(1..50,451..500))
                     /label="order_test"
                     /note="complement-strand order() with boundary-
                     touching parts; must NOT be rewritten as a wrap"
